Room: Room's content-blocking proxy joins every URLLoaderFactory.

Room blocks ads and trackers itself (B-30; research/notes/adblock-approach.md,
option c, the user's decision 2026-10-17): adblock-rust in //room decides
per request, so //room needs to sit between a frame's or worker's
URLLoaderFactory and the network, as the webRequest API and the signin and
enterprise header proxies do.

No existing hook: the interceptors are appended only by
ChromeContentBrowserClient::WillCreateURLLoaderFactory; a ContentBrowserClient
subclass would replace Chrome's for one call, and the webRequest proxy runs
only for extensions. //room appends its proxy when blocking is on (it
forwards every request it does not block to the next factory with the
caller's own client) and never for downloads.

2026-10-17. //room: room/core/content_blocking/network_blocking.cc
(InstallNetworkBlockingHook).
diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 2e0f287290b76..ffe01b75522f7 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -847,6 +847,19 @@ using plugins::ChromeContentBrowserClientPluginsPart;
 using web_app::ChromeContentBrowserClientIsolatedWebAppsPart;
 #endif
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core at startup. Adds Room's content-blocking proxy to
+// the factory (ads and trackers, B-30); it decides per request.
+void (*g_url_loader_factory_hook)(
+    content::BrowserContext*,
+    content::RenderFrameHost*,
+    int,
+    content::ContentBrowserClient::URLLoaderFactoryType,
+    const url::Origin&,
+    const net::IsolationInfo&,
+    network::URLLoaderFactoryBuilder&) = nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 namespace {
 
 const char kAIManagerUserDataKey[] = "ai_manager";
@@ -6865,6 +6878,12 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::WillCreateURLLoaderFactory(
         frame, factory_builder);
   }
 
+  if (room::g_url_loader_factory_hook) {
+    room::g_url_loader_factory_hook(browser_context, frame, render_process_id,
+                                    type, request_initiator, isolation_info,
+                                    factory_builder);
+  }
+
   MaybeSetTargetNetwork(GetBoundNetworkFromRenderFrameHost(frame),
                         factory_builder, is_for_network_service);
 
